  "Question": "What is the smallest possible average of four distinct positive even integers?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(6\\)",
    "E": "\\(7\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Arrange the four integers from smallest to largest. Because they are positive, even, and distinct, they must be at least \\(2,4,6,8\\), respectively. Their sum is therefore at least \\(20\\), so their average is at least\n\\[\n\\frac{2+4+6+8}{4}=5.\n\\]\nThe integers \\(2,4,6,8\\) satisfy every condition and attain this average. Thus the smallest possible average is \\(\\boxed{5}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
